speechtext:
Mr. Speaker, I apologize to the hon. Member;
I should have answered this question yesterday. I tabled this morning the Order in Council dealing with the matter of the reference to the Supreme Court covering the 
Pacific coast, and I sent a copy to my right hon. friend and I think to certain other Members. This particular reference was forwarded to the Government of British Columbia for any comment they might wish to make. There is an examination into the question of references covering other coasts in other Provinces, but they will not be made for the time being; there is a good deal of work to be done. In any event, it will be well to find out what the decision may be in respect of the Pacific coast question.
